BE-300 2.4.18: backport the exit_group(2) syscall (alias of sys_exit).

Root cause of the "every dynamically-linked program dies with
Trace/breakpoint trap" failure on the BE-300 2.4.18 + uClibc-ng
userspace (busybox, Opie/qpe, ...):

uClibc-ng 1.0.51's _exit() unconditionally issues syscall 4246
(exit_group), which was added upstream in Linux 2.5.35. Stock 2.4.18
has no such syscall, so the call returns -ENOSYS and uClibc-ng falls
through to its "_exit must never return" guard:

    li   v0, 4246          # __NR_exit_group
    syscall
    ...
    break 0xff             # <- reached on ENOSYS -> SIGTRAP

do_bp() then delivers SIGTRAP, so the shell reports "Trace/breakpoint
trap" for every process that terminates normally. main()/write()/
fprintf() all work — only termination traps — which is why the symptom
looked like a fork/exec or copy_page corruption but was not (a static
bare-syscall binary using __NR_exit (4001) directly works perfectly).

Confirmed empirically: a one-line do_bp printk showed
  comm=test_dyn epc=<libuClibc _exit+0x44> op=00ff000d (break 0xff)
and after this patch the SIGTRAP is gone and qpe/Opie boots through
its full init to mainloop with zero traps.

Fix: register exit_group at its upstream o32 number (__NR_Linux + 246)
pointing at sys_exit. For the BE-300 userspace (busybox single-threaded;
2.4 LinuxThreads are separate tasks anyway) exit_group is semantically
identical to exit. The 4236..4245 gap is filled with sys_ni_syscall and
__NR_Linux_syscalls is bumped so the o32 dispatcher bounds check
(scall_o32.S: sltiu v0, MAX_SYSCALL_NO+1) accepts 4246.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/syscalls.h
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/syscalls.h
@@ -250,3 +250,22 @@
 SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* reserved for removexattr */
 SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* reserved for lremovexattr */
 SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4235 res. for fremovexattr */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4236 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4237 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4238 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4239 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4240 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4241 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4242 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4243 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4244 */
+SYS(sys_ni_syscall, 0)				/* 4245 */
+/*
+ * BE-300 backport: exit_group (added upstream in 2.5.35) aliased to
+ * sys_exit. uClibc-ng 1.0.51's _exit unconditionally uses exit_group;
+ * on a stock 2.4.18 it returns -ENOSYS and uClibc falls through to a
+ * `break 0xff` guard -> SIGTRAP on every program termination. For the
+ * single-threaded (LinuxThreads = separate tasks) BE-300 userspace,
+ * exit_group is semantically identical to exit.
+ */
+SYS(sys_exit, 1)				/* 4246  exit_group */
--- a/include/asm-mips/unistd.h
+++ b/include/asm-mips/unistd.h
@@ -245,11 +245,14 @@
 #define __NR_removexattr		(__NR_Linux + 233)
 #define __NR_lremovexattr		(__NR_Linux + 234)
 #define __NR_fremovexattr		(__NR_Linux + 235)
+/* BE-300 backport: exit_group (upstream 2.5.35) aliased to sys_exit so
+ * uClibc-ng 1.0.51's _exit() works on 2.4.18 (see syscalls.h). */
+#define __NR_exit_group			(__NR_Linux + 246)
 
 /*
  * Offset of the last Linux flavoured syscall
  */
-#define __NR_Linux_syscalls		235
+#define __NR_Linux_syscalls		246
 
 #ifndef _LANGUAGE_ASSEMBLY
 
